WAMR 2.4.5: execute SIMD in the classic interpreter used for legacy EH.

Reuse the fixed-width SIMD operations and SIMDe 0.8.2 dependency from the
fast interpreter, with the classic value stack, original Wasm immediates,
and memory bounds checks. Preserve all four cells through locals, globals,
select/drop, calls, and exception payloads. Copy catch values from the
saved payload to avoid overlap; rethrow reads that payload after the tag.
Do not rewrite v128 locals into the classic interpreter's 32/64-bit fast-local instructions.

LLGo regression: internal/build/testdata/wasm-wasi-simd/classic.wat.

